  {
    "name": "agent_archive",
    "description": "Archive a coding agent's session (from agents_list) when the user asks to archive or tidy up agents: it leaves the Agents list for Archived in Persona, nothing is deleted, and `restore: true` brings it back, reopening nothing on the computer (never remove a session any other way). Persona also asks the agent's own tool to archive it where that tool has an archive (Codex); the result says whether it did (native: done / pending / unsupported). Without close the agent itself is not closed: one open on its computer stays open. With close, its agent and its terminal tab are also closed on its computer (its transcript stays; then it is stopped until resumed): only when the user asks to close it too, and the user confirms in Persona first (declined: nothing changes). A busy agent is refused and nothing changes: working, waiting for an answer or background work, and for close also a /loop, queued messages or a server it runs. When the close does not happen the session stays archived and still open on the computer, and the result says why: tell the user exactly that, not that it was closed. With `force: true`, explicitly cancel and close an Agent stuck waiting for a terminal confirmation, then archive it. Use force only when the user asks to stop or archive that blocked Agent. Pending permissions and plans are rejected or cancelled, never allowed. Working Agents, background work, running subagents/workflows, queued messages, loops and serving ports are still refused. A failed close leaves it visible. Force implies close and does not ask for a second permission card. Not for Persona conversations, which no tool archives.",
