  {
    "name": "persona_settings",
    "description": "This is how the user changes Persona's settings: ask them in conversation, there is no settings page for these. `list` (the default) shows every key with a one-line description, how to set it and its current value (secrets only as set or unset); `get` reads one. `set`, `add` and `remove` apply immediately with before → after; only secret inputs (e.g. adding mail) use a card — never ask for secrets in chat. Change only what was asked. Areas: assistant behavior, session triage, About Me, saved prompts, start page and sidebar, inbox sorting and task links, mail accounts, extensions (`extension.\u003cid\u003e`, channels and connectors too: its own switch, `enabled`, and its settings) and their download mirrors, hub updates, device notifications, each agent CLI's settings per computer and muted Claude config directories. Model profiles are not here: use `model_profiles`.\n\n`test` checks a provider ID for a `model_config.*` group, without approval or saving. `assistant.standing_authorizations`: never invent a quote or widen a grant's scope, and give only conditions that can be checked independently.\n\nDetails: read .claude/skills/persona-work/references/persona-settings.md in your working directory.",
