  {
    "name": "task_plan",
    "description": "Plan code, repository research and other multi-step work for coding Agents, one supervised task per independent piece. Check machines_list and agents_list first; an Agent's own follow-up goes to agent_send. Read-only, user_requested and preapproved tasks start at once, others on the owner's Start; a queued receipt is not a started Agent.\n\nWrite title (under 20 characters), why, goal, done_when and out_of_bounds in Simplified Chinese. A writable task needs checkable done_when, a read-only one goal. Continue a task with continues (scope_revision after task_scope); retry a failed start with task_start_repair retry. readonly=true: Claude-family launchers run with bypassPermissions; Codex and agy (Antigravity companion) in plan mode, or with assistant.readonly_mode=prompt by instruction only, not a security boundary; pi and cursor refuse it.\n\n`wait_seconds` observes up to 50 seconds after dispatch, appending `Inline observation` JSON: `completed`(this input's `reply`), `question`(pending `interaction_id`), `timeout`/`cancelled`/`unavailable`/`interrupted`/`failed`, with known input/session ids. Observation never answers questions, accepts tasks, resends or cancels work; normal supervision/`task_review` applies. Older nodes may time out instead of an unrelated reply. Only an immediately dispatchable single-task plan waits.\n\nDetails: read .claude/skills/persona-work/references/task-plan.md in your working directory.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "tasks"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "wait_seconds": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0,
          "description": "0/omitted: normal receipt"
        },
        "tasks": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "maxItems": 8,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "title",
              "prompt",
              "role",
              "machine",
              "readonly",
              "user_requested",
              "why"
            ],
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "required": [
                  "cwd"
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "workspace",
                  "todo_id"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "workspace": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "backend"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "workspace"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "workspace": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "container"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            ],
            "properties": {
              "title": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "context": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "prompt": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "machine": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "machine_policy": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "fixed",
                  "flexible"
                ]
              },
              "cwd": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "workspace": {
                "type": [
                  "string",
                  "object"
                ],
                "description": "omit for the default; new: an engine-made checkout (never have the Agent run git worktree add); existing + queue: true waits until it is free",
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "new",
                      "none"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "backend"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "backend": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "required": [
                          "operation_id"
                        ],
                        "properties": {
                          "operation_id": {
                            "type": "string"
                          },
                          "host": {
                            "type": "string"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "container"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "container": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "selected_repo_ids": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "minItems": 1,
                            "items": {
                              "type": "string"
                            }
                          },
                          "operation_id": {
                            "type": "string"
                          },
                          "host": {
                            "type": "string"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "existing"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "existing": {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      "queue": {
                        "type": "boolean"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "new"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "new": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "branch": {
                            "type": "string"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "launcher": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "host": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "agy (Antigravity companion) or herdr (terminal); omit to let Persona choose"
              },
              "model": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "permission": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "default",
                  "acceptEdits",
                  "plan",
                  "auto",
                  "bypassPermissions"
                ]
              },
              "role": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "worker",
                  "leader"
                ],
                "description": "leader: its Agent plans and reviews workers"
              },
              "ultracode": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "Claude Code multi-agent workflow for large tasks; slower, costlier"
              },
              "readonly": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "true: no file changes, commits or external writes"
              },
              "user_requested": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "true only if the owner's latest message asked for it"
              },
              "why": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "why this machine, directory and model"
              },
              "done_when": {
                "type": "array",
                "maxItems": 6,
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "goal": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "out_of_bounds": {
                "type": "array",
                "maxItems": 6,
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "continues": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "scope_revision": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "continues_why": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "started_why": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "why you start it unasked"
              },
              "attachments": {
                "type": "array",
                "maxItems": 8,
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "description": "absolute paths of files the owner gave here"
              },
              "expect_minutes": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0
              },
              "project": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "part_of": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "after": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "todo_id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "this chat's open or failed-start to-do with no live Agent"
              },
              "inbox_item": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "tier": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "preset from the snapshot's Model profile line; explicit launcher, model, effort or speed override it"
              },
              "speed": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "standard",
                  "fast",
                  "ultrafast"
                ],
                "description": "standard (default), fast or ultrafast speed; Claude Code: fast only"
              },
              "effort": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "core_rank": 7
  },
  {
    "name": "task_plan_withdraw",
    "description": "Take down a plan card this conversation put up (task_plan) while nothing of it has started: its work was done elsewhere, or the user decided not to do it. The card stops waiting for the user's Start, as when they dismiss it themselves, and leaves the to-handle lists (the snapshot's plans waiting to start, the briefings). Only for a plan of this conversation that still waits for the user's Start; a started or dismissed plan, or another conversation's, is refused and nothing changes. Your reason is kept on record; tell the user in a line which card you took down and why.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "plan_id",
        "reason"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "plan_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the plan's id (plan_…), as task_plan's answer or the snapshot's plans waiting to start give it"
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "why it is no longer needed, in the user's language, one sentence"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "task_review",
    "description": "Record a verdict on a supervised task, judged on its scoped brief and criteria, not the Agent's claims.\n- accepted: with outcome=done, checks holds each done_when criterion once, met, with evidence; user_check waits for the owner's Pass.\n- rework: a concrete next step in note; accept with a note rather than bounce nitpicks.\n- parked: an outside wait, with reason, waiting_on and evidence.\n- needs_user: only what the owner alone can decide, with why_owner, reason, options, recommend and cost_of_waiting.\n- cancelled: duplicate or unwanted tasks only.\nOn another supervisor's task only accept or cancel; send gaps with agent_send.\n\nDetails: read .claude/skills/persona-work/references/task-review.md in your working directory.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "verdict"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "verdict": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "accepted",
            "rework",
            "needs_user",
            "parked",
            "cancelled"
          ]
        },
        "rework_kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "external_input",
            "substantive_new",
            "repeated_error",
            "low_roi_edge"
          ],
          "description": "external_input: not a stalled round; substantive_new: restarts the stalled count"
        },
        "checks": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "criterion",
              "met"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "criterion": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "met": {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              "evidence": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "note": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "in Simplified Chinese: the next step, the decision or the result"
        },
        "outcome": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "done",
            "cannot"
          ]
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "one sentence in the owner's language"
        },
        "waiting_on": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "someone_else",
            "external_event",
            "date"
          ]
        },
        "until": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "3d, 36h or RFC 3339"
        },
        "link": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "recommend": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "why_owner": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "irreversible",
            "visible_to_others",
            "priority",
            "acceptance",
            "only_owner_knows"
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 2,
          "maxItems": 4,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "label",
              "leads_to"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "label": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "leads_to": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "cost_of_waiting": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "question_quote": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the Agent's question verbatim, if reason paraphrases it"
        },
        "can_wait": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "next daily briefing instead of a push"
        },
        "deadline": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "4h, 90m or RFC 3339; needs reversible"
        },
        "also_done": {
          "type": "array",
          "maxItems": 6,
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "user_check": {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "reversible": {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "evidence": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "target",
            "wake",
            "next_actor"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "kind": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "person_reply",
                "merge_review",
                "external_event",
                "date"
              ]
            },
            "target": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 200
            },
            "wake": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 600,
              "description": "the change that ends the wait"
            },
            "next_actor": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "external",
                "owner"
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 2000
            },
            "interaction_id": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 200
            },
            "pr_event": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "terminal",
                "terminal_or_review"
              ]
            },
            "contact": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "channel",
                "url",
                "sender",
                "sent_at",
                "request",
                "status"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "channel": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 100
                },
                "url": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 2000
                },
                "sender": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 200
                },
                "sent_at": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "date-time"
                },
                "request": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 600
                },
                "status": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "sent"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "ready": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "enum": [
                true
              ]
            },
            "reply": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "source",
                "brand",
                "app_id",
                "account_open_id",
                "person_open_id",
                "chat_id",
                "thread_id",
                "request_message_id"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "source": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "larkcli"
                  ]
                },
                "brand": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "feishu",
                    "lark"
                  ]
                },
                "app_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "account_open_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "person_open_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "chat_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "thread_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "request_message_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "description": "person_reply: exact lark-cli ids, not names"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "core_rank": 5
  },
  {
    "name": "task_scope",
    "description": "Change what a supervised task is to do, or what done means, after it started (its todo id). The brief is never rewritten: this adds a brief-log entry (what changed and why), applies the new done_when/expect_minutes, restarts overdue, estimate_due only on a new estimate; the owner reads it in the next digest. It is the only way done_when changes after start (agent_supervise and agent_send on a task use the same log). Give done_when as the whole list after the change: a criterion you leave out is logged as dropped and named in the completion report. A change adding an owner-only step (deploying, merging, releasing, public sends/comments, deleting, spending, production changes) not in the original task is refused unless the owner's own message started this turn: ask first (ask_user, or task_review needs_user), then call again. Only its supervisor may call it; the Agent is not told — send the change with agent_send. estimate_due/overdue: revise expect_minutes here, but a finished task past the settle window with no owner card is refused: give task_review first (accepted/rework/cancelled; needs_user or accepted+user_check if the owner must act); chat-only asks never reach Needs you.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "change",
        "why"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the task's todo id (todo_…)"
        },
        "change": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "what changes, in one sentence the owner can read (Simplified Chinese), e.g. require verification in the test environment only, instead of a staged production rollout"
        },
        "why": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "why, in one sentence (Simplified Chinese)"
        },
        "done_when": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "maxItems": 6,
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "the criteria after the change, the whole list; leave it out to keep them as they are"
        },
        "expect_minutes": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0,
          "description": "how long the task should take from now; leave it out (or 0) to keep it"
        }
      }
    },
    "core_rank": 12
  },
  {
    "name": "task_decided",
    "description": "Record the owner's needs_user choice; main chat or supervisor only. Quote their words and exact option; never guess. told_agent=true means already delivered (also direct Agent chat): record only. Otherwise send and record. Both settle the ask.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "option",
        "said"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "task id"
        },
        "option": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "exact option label"
        },
        "said": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "owner's words"
        },
        "told_agent": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "true: already delivered to the Agent, record only; false: relay and record"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "task_start_repair",
    "description": "Remedy a failed start of one of this conversation's tasks while its computer keeps the tab the agent did not start in (a supervision message says until when). `screen` reads the tab's last 30 lines: the question its shell waits on, or where the agent's screen stopped. `keys` types into it while no agent runs there: `text` as is (no enter, at most 32 characters), then `keys` by name (\"enter\", \"esc\", \"ctrl+c\", \"y\", \"n\", \"up\", \"down\"…, at most 8); read the screen before and after. `retry` starts the agent again, in the kept tab or a new one, or with `launcher` on another launcher of the same computer and workspace; at most 3 retries, the hub never retries itself, and the outcome comes as a supervision message.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "action",
        "todo_id"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "screen",
            "keys",
            "retry"
          ],
          "description": "read the kept tab, type into it, or start the agent again"
        },
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the task's id, as the supervision message gives it"
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "keys, retry: why, kept with the task's history"
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 32,
          "description": "text to type as is, before the keys"
        },
        "keys": {
          "type": "array",
          "maxItems": 8,
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "keys to press after the text, by name"
        },
        "launcher": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "optional: another launcher of that computer, as the supervision message lists"
        },
        "model": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "with launcher: a model id (default: its own)"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "todo_links",
    "description": "A to-do's saved repository and issue/PR associations. `get` reads them with their revisions; no Git or network call. `add_links` adds 1–50 exact issue or PR URLs as `links` [{url, title}] (actual titles only), grouped by repository by itself. `set` replaces the repositories at once (`expected_revision`, `expected_catalog_revision`, `repositories`; [] removes them) and `set_links` one repository's links (`repo_id`, `expected_revision`, `links`); reread and reconcile on a conflict. The hub already links the issues and PRs an Agent's replies name, and an association never proves completion.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "action",
        "id"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "get",
            "add_links",
            "set",
            "set_links"
          ],
          "description": "get, add issue/PR links, replace the repositories, or replace one repository's links"
        },
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the to-do's id"
        },
        "expected_revision": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "expected_catalog_revision": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "repositories": {
          "type": "array",
          "maxItems": 20,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "repo_id"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "repo_id": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "directory_alias": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "requested_ref": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "kind": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "default",
                      "branch",
                      "tag",
                      "commit",
                      "ref"
                    ]
                  },
                  "value": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1
                  }
                },
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "required": [
                  "kind"
                ],
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "kind": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "const": "default"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "required": [
                      "value"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "links": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "url": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "minLength": 1
                    },
                    "kind": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "enum": [
                        "issue",
                        "pull_request"
                      ]
                    },
                    "number": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "pattern": "^[1-9][0-9]{0,19}$"
                    },
                    "title": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Plain source title; trim; ≤1024 UTF-8 bytes.",
                      "maxLength": 1024
                    }
                  },
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "oneOf": [
                    {
                      "required": [
                        "url"
                      ],
                      "not": {
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "required": [
                              "kind"
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "required": [
                              "number"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "required": [
                        "kind",
                        "number"
                      ],
                      "not": {
                        "required": [
                          "url"
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "maxItems": 50
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          }
        },
        "repo_id": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "links": {
          "type": "array",
          "maxItems": 50,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "url": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "kind": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "issue",
                  "pull_request"
                ]
              },
